    solution_html: `
      <div class="solution-container">
        <h4>Solution to Question 7: Expected Cash Flow, ENPV, Variance, and Standard Deviation</h4>
        
        <p><strong>(a) Computation of Expected Net Cash Flow (ENCF):</strong></p>
        <p>$$\text{ENCF} = \sum_{i=1}^n (P_i \times \text{CF}_i)$$</p>
        <p>$$\text{ENCF} = (0.25 \times 20,00,000) + (0.50 \times 15,00,000) + (0.25 \times 8,00,000)$$</p>
        <p>$$\text{ENCF} = 5,00,000 + 7,50,000 + 2,00,000 = \mathbf{₹ 14,50,000}$$</p>

        <p><strong>(b) Computation of Expected Net Present Value (ENPV):</strong></p>
        <p>$$\text{PV of ENCF} = \frac{\text{ENCF}}{1 + k} = \frac{14,50,000}{1.10} = ₹ 13,18,181.82$$</p>
        <p>$$\text{ENPV} = \text{PV of Cash Inflows} - \text{Initial Outlay}$$</p>
        <p>$$\text{ENPV} = ₹ 13,18,181.82 - ₹ 12,00,000 = \mathbf{₹ 1,18,181.82}$$</p>

        <p><strong>(c) Computation of Variance ($sigma^2$) and Standard Deviation ($sigma$):</strong></p>
        <table class="exam-table" border="1" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; margin: 15px 0;">
          <thead style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <tr>
              <th style="text-align: left;">State</th>
              <th style="text-align: right;">$	ext{CF}_i$ (₹)</th>
              <th style="text-align: right;">$	ext{ENCF}$ (₹)</th>
              <th style="text-align: right;">Deviation $(	ext{CF}_i - 	ext{ENCF})$ (₹)</th>
              <th style="text-align: right;">$(	ext{CF}_i - 	ext{ENCF})^2$ (₹$^2$)</th>
              <th style="text-align: center;">$P_i$</th>
              <th style="text-align: right;">$P_i \times (\text{CF}_i - \text{ENCF})^2$ (₹$^2$)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Boom</td>
              <td style="text-align: right;">20,00,000</td>
              <td style="text-align: right;">14,50,000</td>
              <td style="text-align: right;">+ 5,50,000</td>
              <td style="text-align: right;">3,02,50,00,00,000</td>
              <td style="text-align: center;">0.25</td>
              <td style="text-align: right;">75,62,50,00,000</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Normal</td>
              <td style="text-align: right;">15,00,000</td>
              <td style="text-align: right;">14,50,000</td>
              <td style="text-align: right;">+ 50,000</td>
              <td style="text-align: right;">2,50,00,00,000</td>
              <td style="text-align: center;">0.50</td>
              <td style="text-align: right;">1,25,00,00,000</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Recession</td>
              <td style="text-align: right;">8,00,000</td>
              <td style="text-align: right;">14,50,000</td>
              <td style="text-align: right;">- 6,50,000</td>
              <td style="text-align: right;">4,22,50,00,00,000</td>
              <td style="text-align: center;">0.25</td>
              <td style="text-align: right;">1,05,62,50,00,000</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="font-weight: bold; background-color: #fafafa;">
              <td colspan="6" style="text-align: right;">Variance ($sigma^2$):</td>
              <td style="text-align: right;">1,82,50,00,00,000 ₹$^2$</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>$$\mathbf{\text{Variance } (\sigma^2) = 1.825 \times 10^{11} \text{ ₹}^2 = 18.25 \text{ (in Lakhs)}^2}$$</p>
        <p>$$\mathbf{\text{Standard Deviation } (\sigma) = \sqrt{1,82,50,00,00,000} = ₹ 4,27,200.19 \approx ₹ 4,27,200}$$</p>
      </div>
    `
