    solution_html: `
      <div class="solution-container">
        <h4>Solution to Question 7: Single Index Model Risk Decomposition</h4>
        
        <p><strong>(a) Systematic Risk of Security P:</strong></p>
        <p>Under Sharpe's Single Index Model, systematic risk is that portion of total variance driven by exposure to market movements:</p>
        <p>$$	ext{Systematic Risk} = eta_P^2 	imes sigma_M^2$$</p>
        <p>Given $eta_P = 1.25$ and $sigma_M^2 = 225$:</p>
        <p>$$	ext{Systematic Risk} = (1.25)^2 	imes 225 = 1.5625 	imes 225 = mathbf{351.5625}$$</p>

        <p><strong>(b) Unsystematic (Firm-Specific) Risk:</strong></p>
        <p>Unsystematic risk is the residual variance ($sigma_{eP}^2$) unique to the firm:</p>
        <p>$$	ext{Unsystematic Risk} = sigma_{eP}^2 = (8.00)^2 = mathbf{64.00}$$</p>

        <p><strong>(c) Total Risk (Total Variance and Standard Deviation):</strong></p>
        <p>$$	ext{Total Variance } (sigma_P^2) = 	ext{Systematic Risk} + 	ext{Unsystematic Risk}$$</p>
        <p>$$sigma_P^2 = 351.5625 + 64.00 = mathbf{415.5625}$$</p>
        <p>Total Standard Deviation ($sigma_P$):</p>
        <p>$$sigma_P = sqrt{415.5625} = mathbf{20.39%}$$</p>

        <p><strong>(d) Coefficient of Determination ($R^2$) and Financial Interpretation:</strong></p>
        <p>$$R^2 = rac{	ext{Systematic Risk}}{	ext{Total Risk}} = rac{351.5625}{415.5625} = mathbf{0.8460 	ext{ (or 84.60%)}}$$</p>
        <div class="summary-box" style="background-color: #f9f9f9; padding: 12px; border-left: 4px solid #2196F3; margin-top: 15px;">
          <strong>Financial Interpretation:</strong> $R^2 = 84.60%$ indicates that 84.60% of the total price volatility of Security P is directly explained by macroeconomic market fluctuations. The remaining $15.40%$ ($1 - R^2$) represents unsystematic risk arising from company-specific factors, which can be eliminated through portfolio diversification.
        </div>
      </div>
    `
