      <div class="question-container">
        <p>The regulatory and statutory architecture governing securitization in India has evolved significantly. With reference to the Indian legal regime:</p>
        <ol type="a">
          <li>Explain the core objectives of the <strong>SARFAESI Act, 2002</strong>, and outline the extraordinary enforcement powers conferred on secured creditors under <strong>Section 13</strong> without court intervention.</li>
          <li>State the taxation framework applicable to Securitization Trusts under <strong>Section 115TCA</strong> of the Income-tax Act, 1961.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
