    question_html: `<p><strong>Question 14 [Practical &mdash; 8 Marks]</strong></p>
<p><strong>Zenith AgriTech Solutions Pvt. Ltd.</strong> raised <strong>₹1.50 Crore</strong> from an angel syndicate on April 1, 2025 by issuing a Convertible Promissory Note with the following contractual covenants:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Simple Interest Rate: <strong>10.0% per annum</strong>.</li>
  <li>Maturity Period: 18 Months (October 1, 2026).</li>
  <li>Valuation Cap: <strong>₹12.00 Crore</strong>.</li>
  <li>Conversion Discount: <strong>20.0%</strong>.</li>
  <li>Conversion Trigger: Automatic conversion upon the closing of a Series A Qualified Financing Round of at least ₹5.00 Crore.</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Series A Qualified Financing Round (October 1, 2026 &mdash; exactly 18 months later):</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>An institutional venture capital fund ("Peak Ventures") infuses <strong>₹8.00 Crore</strong> in cash at a pre-money equity valuation of <strong>₹20.00 Crore</strong>.</li>
  <li>The company had <strong>40,00,000 (40 Lakh) fully paid equity shares</strong> held by founders prior to the Series A round.</li>
  <li>Series A Issue Price per Share = $\frac{₹20,00,00,000}{40,00,000} = \mathbf{₹50.00 \text{ per share}}$.</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Required:</strong></p>
<ol type="1">
  <li>Compute the total convertible principal and accrued interest amount available for conversion on October 1, 2026.</li>
  <li>Compute the conversion price per share under:
    <ol type="a">
      <li>The <strong>Conversion Discount Method</strong>.</li>
      <li>The <strong>Valuation Cap Method</strong>.</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
  <li>Identify which conversion mechanism governs the angel syndicate's conversion, and state the governing price per share and effective discount percentage realized.</li>
  <li>Compute the total number of equity shares issued to the angel syndicate upon note conversion.</li>
  <li>Compute the number of shares issued to the Series A investor (Peak Ventures) and prepare the Post-Series A Capitalization Table detailing the final shareholding and percentage ownership of Founders, Angel Syndicate, and Peak Ventures.</li>
</ol>`,
    solution_html: `<p><strong>Solution 14: Convertible Note Conversion Mechanics &amp; Post-Series A Cap Table</strong></p>

<p><strong>1. Computation of Convertible Amount (Principal + Accrued Interest):</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>Principal Note Amount = ₹1.50 Crore (₹150.00 Lakh).</li>
  <li>Note Tenure = 18 months = 1.5 years; Simple Interest = 10.0% p.a.</li>
  <li>$$\text{Accrued Interest} = ₹150.00 \text{ Lakh} \times 10.0\% \times 1.5 \text{ years} = \mathbf{₹22.50 \text{ Lakh}}$$</li>
  <li>$$\text{Total Convertible Debt Balance} = ₹150.00 \text{ Lakh} + ₹22.50 \text{ Lakh} = \mathbf{₹172.50 \text{ Lakh}} \quad (₹1.725 \text{ Crore})$$</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>2. Conversion Price Computation under Both Mechanisms:</strong></p>
<ol type="a">
  <li><strong>Under Conversion Discount Method (20% Discount):</strong>
    $$P_{\text{discount}} = \text{Series A Price} \times (1 - 0.20) = ₹50.00 \times 0.80 = \mathbf{₹40.00 \text{ per share}}$$
  </li>
  <li><strong>Under Valuation Cap Method:</strong>
    $$P_{\text{cap}} = \frac{\text{Valuation Cap}}{\text{Pre-Money Shares}} = \frac{₹12,00,00,000}{40,00,000 \text{ shares}} = \mathbf{₹30.00 \text{ per share}}$$
  </li>
</ol>

<p><strong>3. Governing Conversion Price &amp; Effective Discount:</strong></p>
<p>The investor is entitled to convert at the lower price:</p>
<p>$$\mathbf{P_{\text{conversion}} = \min(₹40.00, ₹30.00) = ₹30.00 \text{ per share}}$$</p>
<p><em>Conclusion:</em> The <strong>Valuation Cap governs</strong> the conversion. The angel syndicate realizes an effective discount of:</p>
<p>$$\text{Effective Discount} = \frac{₹50.00 - ₹30.00}{₹50.00} \times 100 = \mathbf{40.0\%}$$</p>

<p><strong>4. Number of Shares Issued to Angel Syndicate:</strong></p>
<p>$$\text{Shares Issued to Angels} = \frac{\text{Total Convertible Debt Balance}}{\text{Governing Price}} = \frac{₹1,72,50,000}{₹30.00} = \mathbf{5,75,000 \text{ equity shares}}$$</p>

<p><strong>5. Series A Shares Issued and Post-Money Cap Table:</strong></p>
<p>$$\text{Shares Issued to Peak Ventures} = \frac{\text{Series A Investment}}{\text{Series A Price}} = \frac{₹8,00,00,000}{₹50.00} = \mathbf{16,00,000 \text{ equity shares}}$$</p>

<div class="table-responsive">
  <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">
    <thead class="table-dark">
      <tr>
        <th>Shareholder Group</th>
        <th class="text-end">Number of Shares</th>
        <th class="text-end">Equity Ownership %</th>
        <th class="text-end">Value @ ₹50/sh (₹ Cr)</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Founders (Pre-Series A Equity)</td>
        <td class="text-end">40,00,000</td>
        <td class="text-end">64.78%</td>
        <td class="text-end">₹20.000</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Angel Syndicate (Note Conversion @ ₹30/sh)</td>
        <td class="text-end">5,75,000</td>
        <td class="text-end">9.31%</td>
        <td class="text-end">₹2.875</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Peak Ventures (Series A Round @ ₹50/sh)</td>
        <td class="text-end">16,00,000</td>
        <td class="text-end">25.91%</td>
        <td class="text-end">₹8.000</td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="table-success">
        <td><strong>Total Post-Series A Capitalization</strong></td>
        <td class="text-end"><strong>61,75,000</strong></td>
        <td class="text-end"><strong>100.00%</strong></td>
        <td class="text-end"><strong>₹30.875 Crore</strong></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p><em>(Note: Post-Series A total enterprise valuation equals $61,75,000 \text{ shares} \times ₹50.00 = \mathbf{₹30.875 \text{ Crore}}$).</em></p>`
