    question_html: `<p><strong>Question 17 [Practical &mdash; 8 Marks]</strong></p>
<p><strong>Nexus Robotics Pvt. Ltd.</strong> completed its Series A funding two years ago, but now faces a challenging market downturn forcing it to raise a <strong>Series B Down-Round</strong>:</p>

<p><strong>Historical Series A Capitalization:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>Founders hold: <strong>40,00,000 Common Shares</strong>.</li>
  <li>Series A Investor ("Alpha Capital") invested <strong>₹10.00 Crore</strong> at an original purchase price of <strong>₹100.00 per share</strong>, receiving <strong>10,00,000 Series A Preferred Shares</strong> (convertible 1:1 into common shares).</li>
  <li>Total pre-Series B shares = 50,00,000 shares.</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Series B Down-Round Terms:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>A distressed turnaround venture fund ("Beta Horizon") agrees to infuse <strong>₹6.00 Crore</strong> at a depressed price of <strong>₹60.00 per share</strong>, receiving <strong>10,00,000 newly issued Series B Preferred Shares</strong>.</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Required:</strong></p>
<ol type="1">
  <li>If Alpha Capital holds <strong>Full Ratchet Anti-Dilution Protection</strong>:
    <ol type="a">
      <li>Determine the revised conversion price for Series A shares.</li>
      <li>Compute the new conversion ratio and total common shares to which Alpha Capital becomes entitled upon conversion.</li>
      <li>Compute the post-Series B fully diluted shareholding and ownership percentage of the Founders.</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
  <li>If Alpha Capital holds <strong>Broad-Based Weighted Average Anti-Dilution Protection</strong> using the standard NVCA formula:
    $$	ext{CP}_2 = 	ext{CP}_1 	imes rac{A + B}{A + C}$$
    Where:
    <ul>
      <li>$	ext{CP}_1$ = Original Series A conversion price (₹100.00)</li>
      <li>$A$ = Pre-round fully diluted common shares outstanding (50,00,000 shares)</li>
      <li>$B$ = Number of shares that would have been purchased at the original price ($rac{	ext{Series B Capital}}{	ext{CP}_1} = rac{₹6,00,00,000}{₹100.00} = 6,00,000 	ext{ shares}$)</li>
      <li>$C$ = Actual number of shares issued in the down-round (10,00,000 shares)</li>
    </ul>
    <ol type="a">
      <li>Compute the revised conversion price ($	ext{CP}_2$) for Series A shares.</li>
      <li>Compute the new conversion ratio and total common shares to which Alpha Capital becomes entitled.</li>
      <li>Compute the post-Series B fully diluted shareholding and ownership percentage of the Founders.</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
  <li>Compare the Founders' retained ownership percentage under both mechanisms, quantifying the dilution penalty of Full Ratchet protection.</li>
</ol>`,
    solution_html: `<p><strong>Solution 17: Mathematical Modeling of Full Ratchet vs. Broad-Based Weighted Average Anti-Dilution</strong></p>

<p><strong>1. Evaluation under Full Ratchet Anti-Dilution:</strong></p>
<ol type="a">
  <li><strong>Revised Conversion Price:</strong>
    Under Full Ratchet, the conversion price drops completely to the down-round price:
    $$\mathbf{\text{CP}_{\text{Full Ratchet}} = ₹60.00 \text{ per share}}$$
  </li>
  <li><strong>Conversion Ratio and Adjusted Common Shares:</strong>
    $$\text{New Conversion Ratio} = \frac{\text{Original Price}}{\text{Revised Conversion Price}} = \frac{₹100.00}{₹60.00} = \mathbf{1.6667}$$
    $$\text{Adjusted Common Shares for Alpha Capital} = 10,00,000 \times 1.6667 = \mathbf{16,66,667 \text{ shares}}$$
    <em>(Alpha Capital receives an extra 6,66,667 compensatory shares for zero cash!).</em>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Post-Series B Cap Table (Full Ratchet):</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Founders: 40,00,000 shares</li>
      <li>Series A (Alpha Capital): 16,66,667 shares</li>
      <li>Series B (Beta Horizon): 10,00,000 shares</li>
      <li>$$\text{Total Fully Diluted Shares} = 40,00,000 + 16,66,667 + 10,00,000 = \mathbf{66,66,667 \text{ shares}}$$</li>
      <li>$$\text{Founders' Ownership \%} = \frac{40,00,000}{66,66,667} = \mathbf{60.00\%}$$</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ol>

<p><strong>2. Evaluation under Broad-Based Weighted Average Anti-Dilution:</strong></p>
<ol type="a">
  <li><strong>Revised Conversion Price ($	ext{CP}_2$):</strong>
    $$	ext{CP}_2 = 	ext{CP}_1 	imes rac{A + B}{A + C} = ₹100.00 	imes rac{50,00,000 + 6,00,000}{50,00,000 + 10,00,000}$$
    $$	ext{CP}_2 = ₹100.00 	imes rac{56,00,000}{60,00,000} = ₹100.00 	imes 0.933333 = \mathbf{₹93.3333 \text{ per share}}$$
  </li>
  <li><strong>Conversion Ratio and Adjusted Common Shares:</strong>
    $$\text{New Conversion Ratio} = \frac{₹100.00}{₹93.3333} = \mathbf{1.071429}$$
    $$\text{Adjusted Common Shares for Alpha Capital} = 10,00,000 \times 1.071429 = \mathbf{10,71,429 \text{ shares}}$$
    <em>(Alpha Capital receives 71,429 compensatory adjustment shares).</em>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Post-Series B Cap Table (Broad-Based Weighted Average):</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Founders: 40,00,000 shares</li>
      <li>Series A (Alpha Capital): 10,71,429 shares</li>
      <li>Series B (Beta Horizon): 10,00,000 shares</li>
      <li>$$\text{Total Fully Diluted Shares} = 40,00,000 + 10,71,429 + 10,00,000 = \mathbf{60,71,429 \text{ shares}}$$</li>
      <li>$$\text{Founders' Ownership \%} = \frac{40,00,000}{60,71,429} = \mathbf{65.88\%}$$</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ol>

<p><strong>3. Comparison of Founder Dilution:</strong></p>
<div class="table-responsive">
  <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">
    <thead class="table-dark">
      <tr>
        <th>Stakeholder</th>
        <th class="text-end">Pre-Series B %</th>
        <th class="text-end">Full Ratchet %</th>
        <th class="text-end">Broad-Based Weighted Average %</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Founders</td>
        <td class="text-end">80.00%</td>
        <td class="text-end"><strong>60.00%</strong></td>
        <td class="text-end"><strong>65.88%</strong></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Series A (Alpha Capital)</td>
        <td class="text-end">20.00%</td>
        <td class="text-end">25.00%</td>
        <td class="text-end">17.65%</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Series B (Beta Horizon)</td>
        <td class="text-end">&mdash;</td>
        <td class="text-end">15.00%</td>
        <td class="text-end">16.47%</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p><strong>Dilution Penalty:</strong> Under Full Ratchet, the founders are penalized by an additional <strong>5.88% loss of company equity</strong> (retaining only 60.00% vs. 65.88%), as Series A gains 5,95,238 more shares than under weighted average. This highlights why founders vigorously resist Full Ratchet provisions during Series A term sheet negotiations.</p>`
